claim.claim-text:
coating at least one of said carbon-carbon (C/C) composite valve stem and valve head with a high temperature resistant coating comprising an inner layer and an outer layer. 

The method according to claim 7, wherein said method is further characterized by at least one of the following: i) the elongated cylindrical carbon-carbon (C/C) composite valve stem is machined from a densified carbon-carbon (C/C) plate of sufficient thickness; ii) the carbon-carbon (C/C) composite valve stem has a substantially uniform diameter; iii) the carbon-carbon (C/C) plate comprises a plurality of plies of balanced woven fabrics; iv) the carbon-carbon (C/C) plate comprises a plurality of plies of uni- fabric that is unbalanced in fiber volume with a higher fiber volume in the stem axis direction. v) the substantially circular carbon-carbon (C/C) fabric plies are punched out of a carbon-carbon (C/C) prepreg; vi) the substantially circular carbon-carbon (C/C) fabric plies contain carbon powder; vii) the plurality of substantially circular fabric plies are attached to the flared end of said elongated cylindrical carbon-carbon (C/C) composite valve stem; viii) the plurality of substantially circular fabric plies are cure pressed onto the flared end of said elongated cylindrical carbon-carbon (C/C) composite valve stem; ix) the valve head is coated with said high temperature resistant coating; x) both the carbon-carbon (C/C) composite valve stem and valve head are coated with said high temperature resistant coating comprising an inner layer and an outer layer; xi) the high temperature resistant material comprising the inner layer of said coating is selected from the group consisting of nickel, molybdenum, aluminum, aluminum-zinc alloy, nickel aluminide, and iron aluminide; 

 xii) the high temperature resistant material comprising the outer layer of the coating is selected from the group consisting of tungsten carbide, optionally with a cobalt addition; nickel-titanium alloy, optionally with an addition of at least one of chromium, cobalt and yttria; tantalum carbide; and chromium carbide; and xiii) the high temperature resistant coating is resistant to a temperature from about 900°C to about 1500°C.
